<%# Reminder for an account whose address is not confirmed yet (registration
    hardening). Shaped like layouts/_deletion_warning and rendered at the same
    place: the top of the main column, IN the document flow.

    It used to be `fixed top-0` at body level. Out of the flow and with nothing
    compensating its height, it covered the first ~60px of every page — on a
    ticket exactly the row carrying the time-tracking actions, so those buttons
    could be neither seen nor clicked. Do not put the positioning back without
    also reserving the space.

    Not dismissible on purpose: unlike the onboarding banner this one states a
    deadline, and hiding it would let the account expire silently. It disappears
    the moment the address is confirmed. %>
<div class="bg-amber-400 text-black border-2 border-black shadow-lg"
     data-testid="email-confirmation-banner">
  <div class="px-4 py-3">
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-3">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <i class="bi bi-envelope-exclamation-fill text-xl"></i>
        <div class="text-sm">
          <strong><%= t('views.layouts.email_confirmation.title') %></strong>
          <span class="ms-2">
            <%= t('views.layouts.email_confirmation.body', email: current_user.email) %>
            <% if (days = current_user.confirmation_grace_days_left) %>
              <strong><%= t('views.layouts.email_confirmation.days_left', count: days) %></strong>
            <% end %>
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# The banner is where the confusion starts ("what mail?", "which
          address?"), so the answer is one click away right here — same page the
          account form's contextual help opens. %>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 shrink-0">
        <%= link_to t('views.layouts.email_confirmation.why'),
              help_page_url('guides/basics/confirm-email'),
              class: 'text-sm font-semibold underline decoration-2 underline-offset-2 hover:no-underline' %>

        <%= form_with url: user_confirmation_path, method: :post do %>
          <%= hidden_field_tag 'user[email]', current_user.email %>
          <%= render Neo::Buttons::ButtonComponent.new(
                variant: :secondary, size: :medium, tag: :button, type: 'submit',
                icon: 'arrow-repeat'
              ) do %>
            <%= t('views.layouts.email_confirmation.resend') %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
